  "topic_name_ar": "المبني للمجهول في المضارع",
  "topic_name_en": "Passive voice (present)",
  "explanation_content": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "explanation",
        "content_ar": "المبني للمجهول يركّز على الفعل أو متلقي الفعل، وليس على فاعل الفعل. نستخدمه عندما يكون الفاعل غير معروف أو غير مهم، أو عندما نريد التركيز على النتيجة أو العملية.",
        "content_en": "<b>Passive Voice (Present)</b><br><br>Look at these examples:<br>• Coffee <b>is grown</b> in Ethiopia.<br>• Espresso machines <b>are used</b> in Italian cafés.<br>• Turkish coffee <b>is prepared</b> with special techniques.<br><br>In passive voice, we focus on the <i>action</i> or the <i>receiver</i> of the action, not who does it. We use passive voice when:<br>• The doer is unknown or not important<br>• We want to focus on the result/process<br>• In formal writing or scientific descriptions<br><br><b>Formation:</b> Subject + am/is/are + past participle<br><br>The past participle is usually the same as the past simple for regular verbs (work→worked), but irregular verbs have special forms (make→made, grow→grown)."
      },
      {
        "type": "formula",
        "content": "Subject + am/is/are + past participle"
      },
      {
        "type": "examples",
        "items": [
          {
            "sentence": "Coffee is grown in many countries.",
            "highlight": "is grown",
            "translation_ar": "تُزرع القهوة في دول كثيرة"
          },
          {
            "sentence": "Cappuccinos are made with steamed milk.",
            "highlight": "are made",
            "translation_ar": "يُصنع الكابتشينو بالحليب المبخّر"
          },
          {
            "sentence": "The beans are roasted at high temperatures.",
            "highlight": "are roasted",
            "translation_ar": "تُحمص الحبوب في درجات حرارة عالية"
          },
          {
            "sentence": "Fair trade coffee is sold in supermarkets.",
            "highlight": "is sold",
            "translation_ar": "تُباع قهوة التجارة العادلة في السوبر ماركت"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "common_mistakes",
        "items": [
          {
            "wrong": "Coffee is grow in Brazil.",
            "correct": "Coffee is grown in Brazil.",
            "explanation_ar": "استخدم past participle وليس المصدر"
          },
          {
            "wrong": "Lattes are make with milk.",
            "correct": "Lattes are made with milk.",
            "explanation_ar": "الفعل غير النظامي make يصبح made"
          },
          {
            "wrong": "Coffee beans is processed carefully.",
            "correct": "Coffee beans are processed carefully.",
            "explanation_ar": "beans جمع، لذا نستخدم are"
          },
          {
            "wrong": "Turkish coffee prepared with sugar.",
            "correct": "Turkish coffee is prepared with sugar.",
            "explanation_ar": "لا تنس فعل المساعدة am/is/are"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
